/// `OnPlay` opens a surfacing select (e.g. SecretTechnique fetching a Skill
/// when several Skills sit in the draw pile) FULLY RESOLVES — the fetched
/// Skill leaves the draw pile — before the loop's next `StableShuffle` reads
/// it. The Rust auto-play primitive surfaces that select to the harness and
/// stashes a `pending_autoplay_resume` marker; here we detect the suspend and
/// record the not-yet-run iteration COUNT on it (the loop re-selects from the
/// live draw, so the remainder can NOT be a fixed card list). The resolver
/// (`resolve_choice_action`) then re-enters [`catastrophe_resume`] once the
/// pick lands, replaying the remaining iterations against the updated draw
